  "description": "A safe's password consists of `n` digits, each in `[0, k - 1]`. After each digit is entered, the safe checks whether the most recent `n` digits equal the password.\n\nReturn the lexicographically smallest string among all minimum-length strings that unlock the safe for every possible password. Equivalently, every possible `n`-digit password must occur as a contiguous substring. The returned string may use only digits in `[0, k - 1]`.\n\n## Examples\n\n### Example 1\n\n```text\nInput: n = 1, k = 2\nOutput: \"01\"\n```\n\n### Example 2\n\n```text\nInput: n = 2, k = 2\nOutput: \"00110\"\n```\n\n## Constraints\n\n- 1 <= n <= 4\n- 1 <= k <= 10\n- 1 <= k^n <= 4096\n",
